{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/282489-can-geists-be-bound","id":282489,"title":"Can Geists be bound?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-15T10:49:37-07:00","id":282489,"title":"Can Geists be bound?","content":"I have an idea for an antagonist for an upcoming chronicle. It all is based on a Geist being bound like any other ghost. I was wondering if a powerful enough mage could bind one. The mage would be a Tremere Lich. The basic idea is that, since Sin-Eaters can die, the Geist would be yanked and bound. Then, when the Geist finds a new body, that person is then brought to the Tremere who would mind-whammy it into obeying them.<br /> Now, I am fully aware I can just ST fiat this, but I like to adhere to RAW as much as I can. So, it is possible within the rules or does it take, ultimately, me hand-waving it as part of the story? The end result will be what I stated (Geist serving Tremere) since I follow the Golden Rule (Story trumps rules everytime). I was just hoping to, as I said, not just making it ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:11:18-07:00","id":282624,"title":"","content":"Geist can't be bound while in Sin-Eaters, but assumedly can the rest of the time. A Bound Geist can try to influence their Sin-Eater to do what the Lich wants, but can't control them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:16:45-07:00","id":282631,"title":"","content":"I would say they certainly can. The Spirit Arcanum grants Mages powers over both Spirits (of the shadow) and Ghosts, and the Geist core book suggests that a Geist is formed by a ghost merging with a spirit. So it would seem that a Mage with a high enough spirit arcanum should be able to do this using Bind Spirit (Spirit 4). However if I were running it I would add in some complication, perhaps the Mage performing the binding ritual needs access to the Geist's anchor. Or if you're not opposed to a little crossover, perhaps to bind such a spirit you would need the aid of someone with either a special connection to the Shadow (i.e. a Werewolf) or to the Underworld (i.e. a Sin-Eater)<br /> <br /> Edit: Even when a Geist is joined with a Sin-Eater they could possibly still be vulnerable. The Tremere could use a conjunctional Death &amp; Spirit spell (or a special attainment) to sever the Sin-Eater's soul and yank out the Geist along with it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","user":"Aurumae","date":". 10-15-2014, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T12:00:18-07:00","id":285190,"title":"","content":"For Mages to effect Geists, they need the required level of Arcanums in both Death and Spirit. So for a Tremere to do this, he would probably need both Death 4 and Spirit 4 to bind the Geist. As Samedi said, as long as the Geist is bound to the Sin-Eater, it is not formally possible to effect it. Although if he placed some spell on it while it was un-bound, it might still be compelled to follow the command, although it wouldn't be able to outright force the Sin-Eater to comply.<br /> Depending on how powerful your Tremere is, he might even be able to effect the Geist while it is bound to the Sin-Eater, but that would most likely require Arch-Mastery or such, but if he is powerful enough to do that, I dont see what he would even be needing the Geist for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}